<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 4 Best in Slot Gear list for <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warlock.gif");'></span>
<span class="c9">Demonology Warlock</span> DPS in Wrath of <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36597/the-lich-king">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Lich King</span></a> Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a>. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best In Slot Gear for Demonology Warlock DPS in Phase 4</h2>When gearing, there are a multitude of different things to consider; different talent specializations, your currently equipped gear, and your raid composition all play a key part. The biggest deciding factor of them all is Hit rating - having too much or too little Hit rating from either talents, gems, or buffs will result in you swapping in different pieces of gear or gems to reach the relevant Hit cap. You can learn more about stat caps and priorities by visiting the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/guide/classes/warlock/demonology/dps-stat-priority-attributes-pve">Warlock Stat Priority Guide</a>, but here are some important things to note:<div class="box">
<ul class="first last">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Hit cap</b> is determined by the level of the target, with level 83 raid bosses requiring +17% chance to Hit, while level 80 trash mobs require only +4%.<br/>You should typically gear for bosses, but having a specialized setup for clearing trash may be worthwhile. <a class="disclosure-off" href="javascript:">Click here for a full table</a>
