<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warlock.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Warlock</span></a> specializations benefit from both of the Tier 10 set bonuses. The two-piece bonus results in our filler spells which account for a major part of our damage critting 5% more often. When it comes to the four-piece bonus, each time <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=47811/immolate">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_immolation.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Immolate</span></a> or <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=47843/unstable-affliction">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_unstableaffliction_3.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unstable Affliction</span></a> deals damage it has a 15% chance to increase the damage we and our pets do by 10% for 15 seconds.<br/>
<br/>There are three item-level versions of tier gear in this phase, starting with the 251 item-level version bought with <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=341/emblem-of-frost">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></span></a>. This tier has a layered system, requiring a previous piece and a corresponding mark to upgrade. You can potentially get the Legs and Gloves from the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4603/vault-of-archavon">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Vault of Archavon</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>You are limited in how fast you can obtain the four-piece set bonus due to having a limited amount of <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=341/emblem-of-frost">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></span></a> that you can farm each week. The set-bonus also mostly funnels into your personal throughput and not into any contribution towards your Average <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=47240/demonic-pact">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_demonicpact.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Demonic Pact</span></a> Spell Power. As such it can be worthwile to forgo going for Tier 10 during progression and focussing on off-piece items with a lot of spell power and spirit, increasing your raid contribution at the cost of personal performance. Whether this is worthwile will mostly depend on your raid composition, in other words the amount of casters you got in your raid.<br/>
<br/>You will have to <a href="https://wowsims.github.io/wotlk/warlock/" target="_blank">simulate</a> your setup to determine which upgrades and pieces make the most sense to get first as a lot of this will depend on your current equipment. Alternatively, you can also look over at the results from the <a href="https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1poD9jIP52sE7k7e30PN-5GYuGPU0nR_bPWZt599MGik/edit#gid=1351878064" target="_blank">Warlock Simulation Competition</a> to see various setups and how they fare compared to the absolute best in slot setup.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="gems">Gems</h4>For gemming, you will want to use these slots to balance out your Hit and reach your meta gem requirement. Most often it is not worthwhile to get the gem bonus unless it is a spell damage, hit, or haste bonus. For more in-depth info on gems, see the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/guide/classes/warlock/demonology/dps-enchants-gems-pve">Gem Guide.</a>
