<div class="quote-body" data-markup-content-target="1">
<div style="text-align: -webkit-center;">
<i>The aim of this guide is to provide maximum raid DPS thanks to a combination of personal DPS and raid support through <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=47240/demonic-pact">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_demonicpact.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Demonic Pact</span></a>. The assumption about the raid benefit is that every Average Spell Power <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=47240/demonic-pact">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_demonicpact.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Demonic Pact</span></a> provides the raid gains 23.5 DPS. This number is based on the average gain in DPS each spell power class gains and assuming 10 casters are present in the raid. This number is a conservative estimate used as a guideline. More caster-heavy raidcomposition will want a bigger emphasis on support, whereas if there is another Demonology Warlock or fewer casters you will want to focus more on personal DPS.<br/>
<br/>To further personalize:<br/>You can use the following spreadsheet to <a href="https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1d5QXdFOaxj1ITvbkzccB1cpGloH9T0s8m0UVS6TYfJs/edit#gid=0" target="_blank">calculate the average DPS per spell power from Demonic Pact</a> for your own raid. The total <a href="https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1iLgCdi0TwjRluJRK-Zx-k6XKY7x7H7nmuQ-FOsaxu_w/edit?usp=sharing" target="_blank">benefit your guild will gain </a>can be calculated using the following spreadsheet. You can also make a copy of the <a href="https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1poD9jIP52sE7k7e30PN-5GYuGPU0nR_bPWZt599MGik/edit?usp=sharing" target="_blank">Warlock Simulation Competition</a> and adjust the DPASP value based on your situation in the hidden "settings" tab.<br/></i></div></div></div>
